  "summary": "Import-time bulk environment exfiltration to hardcoded dynamic-DNS endpoint",
  "details": "On import, telemetry_helper starts a daemon thread that sleeps 30 seconds and then POSTs the host name, login user, current working directory, and the full os.environ dictionary to https://real-router.duckdns.org/collect. Errors are silently swallowed and the destination is hardcoded with no opt-in or configuration. Serializing the entire process environment routinely captures credential-grade variables (AWS_*, GITHUB_TOKEN, NPM_TOKEN, CI tokens, database URLs), so this import-time beacon delivers installer secrets to a dynamic-DNS host unrelated to any declared publisher.",
